{{!--
  cargo-about's template for THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.html (see about.toml for how it is run).

  Two parts: the data, fonts and native code that ship inside the app, written out here because
  no crate manifest declares them, then every Rust crate in the graph under the license text it
  ships with. The data section copies crates/poe2-oracle/assets/data/NOTICE,
  crates/item-parser/data/NOTICE, crates/stat-filters/data/NOTICE, crates/trade-client/data/NOTICE
  and crates/poe2-oracle/assets/fonts/OFL-*.txt: regenerating the data from another Exiled
  Exchange 2 commit or RePoE export, or changing a font, changes it here too. The native code is
  the WebView2 loader webview2-com-sys bundles (its x64/WebView2LoaderStatic.lib, linked into the
  MSVC exe) with the WebView2 SDK's LICENSE.txt: a webview2-com update that moves to another SDK
  changes the version here.

  This workspace's own crates (path dependencies: no `source`) are PoE2 Oracle itself, not third
  parties, so they are left out of the crate lists -- together with the license entries only they
  use, which cargo-about builds from the NOTICE files it finds inside them. cargo-about sorts each
  entry's users by package id (git, then path, then registry crates), so an entry with a single
  user that is a path crate has no third-party user at all.
--}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>PoE2 Oracle - third-party notices</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            font-family: "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.45;
            background: #fff;
            color: #1b1b1b;
        }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body {
                background: #16130f;
                color: #e8e2d6;
            }
            a {
                color: #d6b46a;
            }
        }
        main {
            max-width: 860px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 24px;
        }
        h1 {
            margin-bottom: 4px;
        }
        .license {
            margin: 24px 0;
            padding-top: 8px;
            border-top: 1px solid #8884;
        }
        .used-by {
            columns: 2;
            margin: 0 0 12px;
        }
        pre {
            max-height: 320px;
            overflow: auto;
            padding: 12px;
            border: 1px solid #8884;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            font-size: 13px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
